.TH P3M-STATS 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-stats \- age and hot/cold statistics from a p3m-ls catalogue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-stats
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-stats
reads a CSV catalogue produced by
.B "p3m\-ls \-m full"
(or
.BR "\-m standard" ,
for modification-time statistics only) and reports:
.IP \(bu 2
the N most recently accessed files
.RB ( atime ),
the N most recently modified files
.RB ( mtime )
and the N largest files;
.IP \(bu 2
how many files and bytes were last accessed, and last modified, within each
age bracket (1 day, 1 week, 1 month, 3 months, 6 months, 1 year, 2 years,
5 years, older);
.IP \(bu 2
a breakdown of file count and bytes by (lower-cased) extension.
.PP
With no
.IR FILE ,
standard input is read, so
.B "p3m\-ls \-m full /data | p3m\-stats"
works without an intermediate file.
The header row is used to locate the columns by name, so column order does not
matter and extra columns are ignored.
Directory rows are excluded from the report.
.PP
The input is streamed once; only fixed-size histograms, a few bounded top-N
heaps and a bounded extension table are held in memory, so memory use does not
grow with the number of rows.
.PP
Rows that are short or have an unparsable timestamp are skipped and counted;
the report is still produced and the exit status is 1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-top " \fIN\fR"
Length of the most-recently-accessed, most-recently-modified and largest-files
lists (default 20;
.B 0
disables them).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-top\-ext " \fIN\fR"
Number of extensions shown in the breakdown, by bytes (default 20;
.B 0
disables it).
Remaining extensions are summed in an
.B (other)
row; files without an extension appear as
.BR (none) .
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the report to
.I FILE
instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-csv\-summary " FILE"
Also write the age histograms as CSV
.RI ( kind,bucket,files,bytes )
to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-now " TIMESTAMP"
Treat
.I TIMESTAMP
(ISO\ 8601 UTC, for example
.BR 2026\-09\-02T00:00:00Z )
as the current time, for reproducible reports.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the report on standard output (useful with
.B \-o
and
.BR \-\-csv\-summary ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The report was produced but some rows were skipped as malformed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, unreadable input, or input lacking a
.I path
column or any timestamp column.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
p3m\-ls \-m full \-o catalogue.csv /data && p3m\-stats catalogue.csv
p3m\-ls \-m full /data | p3m\-stats \-n 50 \-e 30
p3m\-stats \-q \-\-csv\-summary aging.csv catalogue.csv
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-ls (1)
